  "aboutParagraphs": [
    "Kaposia Park is the South St. Paul championship course — a full 27 holes that plays 9,603 feet at par 91, with elevation, trees, and a layout that's hosted serious competition since it expanded. It's a pay-to-play course at $5 a day with a pro shop at the park.",
    "The course began in 1990 and grew into the 27-hole monster it is today. Every hole asks for a different line, and the back stretch in particular has the length and the trees to punish anything loose.",
    "Winter players know the drill: holes 19–25 get pulled when the snow flies, but the full 27 is the summer experience worth driving for."
  ],
