  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 9 is the longest at Kaposia at 615 feet — a par 4 that rolls with the course's best elevation and demands two clean shots through the trees. It's the hole that defines the championship character of the place: long, fair, and completely unforgiving of anything loose.",
  "localTips": "Pay to play at $5 a day. The full 27 holes is a marathon — bring water and a full bag. In winter, holes 19–25 are pulled from the rotation. The pro shop at the park is worth a stop before your round.",
